# AI debug overlay — cross-environment sync (Cloudflare Pages Function + D1).
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev. In production these are set as Pages
# environment variables in the Cloudflare dashboard (or via wrangler).

# Absolute URL of the deployed annotations endpoint. REQUIRED in local dev so
# localhost talks to the same D1 as production. In production leave unset — the
# client falls back to the same-origin `/api/annotations`.
# VITE_ANNOTATIONS_API=https://your-project.pages.dev/api/annotations

# Soft write-gate. Must match the `ANNOTATIONS_KEY` secret set on the Pages
# project. Optional; if unset the endpoint is open.
# VITE_ANNOTATIONS_KEY=some-shared-string

# ── Cloudflare Worker + D1 setup (one-time) ─────────────────────────────────
# Production is a WORKER (…workers.dev), not Pages. The API lives in
# `worker/index.ts`; the D1 binding is declared in `wrangler.toml` and deploys
# with the Worker — no dashboard binding modal, no API token.
#
#   1. DB already created: vulcan-annotations
#      (id 471d2a9d-1a54-418e-849c-479b85cbd979).
#   2. Load the schema:
#        npx wrangler d1 execute vulcan-annotations --remote --file=./schema.sql
#   3. Deploy: `npx wrangler deploy` (or push — the connected Workers build runs
#      `npm run build` then `wrangler deploy`, which reads wrangler.toml).
#   4. Verify: curl https://vulcan-pizza-lab.zatteo.workers.dev/api/annotations
#      → `[]` (JSON) means the Worker + D1 are live.
#   5. (optional gate) npx wrangler secret put ANNOTATIONS_KEY
#      + set VITE_ANNOTATIONS_KEY (build var) to the same value.
